# Static Deployment

SPRAG already knows how to emit fully static HTML, CSS, and browser assets. The missing piece for docs/blog work was **dynamic route expansion at build time**, which this template now uses for both docs and posts.

## Build

```bash
sprag build
```

Deploy the generated `dist/public/` directory.

## GitHub Pages

This template is designed to work when the site lives under a project subpath as well as at the root of a domain.

## What stays interactive?

Anything that is purely client-owned still works on a static host:

- local `Module` state
- delegated DOM events
- hydrated Components that do not call server actions

For that pattern, see the `/playground` route in this template.
